    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302-a10">

                <pb facs="0498" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg428"/>

                <head>Mr. Otterbourg to General
                        O’Horan</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 6, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Esteemed Sir:</hi> I again trouble you with the
                    request to give a passport to go and return to Mr. Robert Beckman, whom I am
                    interested in sending to Tacubaya on account of a private matter which has no
                    connection with the political situation of this capital.</p>
                <p>Mr. Beckman is accompanied by his servant, John Rodriguez.</p>
                <p>Hoping that you will excuse this interruption of your very important occupations,
                    I am, general, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MARCUS OTTERBOURG, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Consul.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas O’Horan,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Political Prefect.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
